## 15. Important Financial Rules

Implement these rules throughout the application.

1. Creating a project increases booked business and receivables, not available funds.
2. Recording a payment increases collected payments and reduces outstanding receivables.
3. Payments credited directly to Payoneer increase only the selected Payoneer balance.
4. Payments received through Fiverr increase the associated Fiverr balance.
5. The client's linked Fiverr account is automatically assigned to newly created projects.
6. Changing the client's linked Fiverr account must not rewrite historical projects.
7. Transfers reduce the source account and increase the destination account by their respective amounts.
8. Fiverr-to-Fiverr transfers are prohibited.
9. Payoneer-to-Payoneer transfers are allowed.
10. Fiverr-to-Payoneer transfers are allowed.
11. Internal transfers never count as new company revenue.
12. Same-currency transfer differences must be recorded as deductions, fees, or adjustments.
13. Currency conversions must show effective rates.
14. Manual balance changes must generate traceable adjustment records.
15. Expenses must decrease the account used to pay them.
16. Fees must not be counted multiple times.
17. Historical balances must be calculated from dated financial records.
18. All financial changes must be saved persistently.
19. Dashboard charts must never rely on fake or hardcoded numbers.
20. Transactions must be validated and saved atomically wherever multiple financial records are affected.

