## 17. Database and Backend Requirements

Use a reliable persistent relational database such as PostgreSQL through Supabase.

The application must store all manually entered information.

Recommended database entities:

- Admin
- Clients
- Projects
- Financial Accounts
- Client Payments
- Account Transactions
- Transfers
- Transfer Fees
- Expense Categories
- Expenses
- Exchange Rates
- Balance Adjustments
- Audit Logs
- Settings

### Database Relationships

- One client can have many projects.
- Each client has one default linked Fiverr account.
- Each project stores its linked Fiverr account.
- Each project can receive multiple payments.
- Payments may be credited to Fiverr or directly to Payoneer.
- One account can have many transactions.
- Transfers connect one source account with one destination account.
- Expenses reference the account that paid them.
- Balance adjustments belong to a financial account.

Use foreign keys and database constraints.

Financial amounts must use decimal-safe storage and calculations.

Never rely on frontend state alone for financial consistency.

All transfers and balance-changing transactions should be handled through server-side transactional operations.

